chars.txt is a copy/paste of charsData so that there is no weird code that would prevent the file to be a proper utf-8 format.
table.txt is the list of wubi codes from ibus-t9
output.txt is just a list of characters (one by line)

chars.txt and table.txt can be replaced by the intermediary databases run

./build_db.py chars.txt table.txt output.txt result.db
  creates a database with the content of chars.txt

cedict_chars.txt is a list of all characters used in Cedict, generated by:
sqlite3 cedict_db 'select hanzi from char_pinyin group by hanzi;' > cedict_chars.txt

